# Subagent model policy

Canonical policy: `~/.cursor/rules/subagent-grok-4.6-high.mdc` and `~/.cursor/AGENTS.md`. Restated here so workspace agents cannot miss it.

When the user does **not** specify a model, all Task/subagent work MUST use **Grok 4.6 High** only: Cursor Task slug `cursor-grok-4.6-high`; Silver Bullet `subagent_type` `sb-grok-4-6-high`. Human names: Grok 4.6 High / Cursor Grok 4.6 High.

Do **not** use Grok 4.6 Extra High / XHigh (`cursor-grok-4.6-xhigh`, `sb-grok-4-6-xhigh`, `*-xhigh*` for Grok 4.6) as the unspecified default or as a “best Grok” substitute. Multiple benchmarks show Grok 4.6 High outperforms Grok 4.6 Extra High.

Fast remains forbidden (`no-fast-mode.mdc`). If High is rejected, use the closest **non-Fast, non-XHigh** Grok 4.6 slug — never Fast, never XHigh as a “higher/better” fallback.

User-named families (RFL GPT/Claude/OpenCode, visual Gemini, etc.) still win. An **explicit** Extra High/XHigh request is followed (do not silently remap). Unspecified default and “use the best Grok” substitutions stay High.

```
❌ BAD — Task model: cursor-grok-4.6-xhigh or cursor-grok-4.6-medium (unspecified)
✅ GOOD — Task model: cursor-grok-4.6-high
```
